**Plan:** parse `--json` in `main`, and print `JSON.stringify(buildRows())` instead of `toTable(...)` when set.

```js
function main(argv) {
  const command = argv[0];
  const json = argv.includes('--json');
  if (command !== 'report') {
    process.stderr.write(USAGE + '\n');
    return 1;
  }
  const rows = buildRows();
  process.stdout.write((json ? JSON.stringify(rows) : toTable(rows)) + '\n');
  return 0;
}
```

`buildRows()` in `[report.js](src/report.js:11)` already returns the full data set, so no changes needed there. Just wire the flag through `[cli.js](src/cli.js:8)`.

